<article class="env-remark" id="0GE2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GE2">Remark <span data-tag="0GE2">98.25.1</span> <span class="named">(Warning)</span>.</a>  The site $(\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\tau $ does not have fibre products. Hence we have to be careful in working with sheaves. For example, the continuous inclusion functor $(\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\tau \to (\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau $ does not define a morphism of sites. See Examples, Section <a href="/tag/0GE8" data-tag="0GE8">110.61</a> for an example in case $\tau = fppf$. </p>
</article>